IMPORTANT: This must be a REAL, FUNCTIONAL BLOGGING PLATFORM

Shankie's should not just be a collection of pre-made mockup pages.

I should be able to use the website myself and continuously add new content without editing the source code.

Think of it as my personal digital magazine + blog + scrapbook CMS.

I need an admin/dashboard system where I can create, edit, publish, draft, and delete content.

Blog creation

I should be able to:

Create a new blog post
Give it a title
Add a cover image
Write the article
Format text
Add headings
Add images between paragraphs
Add videos
Add GIFs
Add links
Add quotes
Add captions
Add stickers/decorations
Add tags/categories
Set a publication date
Save as draft
Preview before publishing
Publish
Edit existing posts
Delete posts

The blog editor should not look like a boring corporate CMS.

The editor itself can be relatively practical, but the final published article must automatically use the Shankie's magazine/scrapbook aesthetic.

MEDIA UPLOADS

I need to be able to upload my own media.

Support:

JPG
PNG
WEBP
GIF
MP4
audio files
PDFs where appropriate

I should be able to upload:

photographs
scans of diary pages
magazine clippings
artwork
screenshots
moodboards
videos
music/audio
stickers
GIFs

Create a Media Library where I can see everything I've uploaded and reuse media in different posts.

Images should automatically be optimized and displayed properly without requiring me to manually code anything.

DIFFERENT TYPES OF CONTENT

Don't restrict the site to traditional blog posts.

I should be able to create different content types such as:

Blog Post

Long-form writing, essays, stories, reflections, etc.

Photo Dump

A scrapbook-style gallery where I can upload multiple photographs and arrange them into a collage.

Playlist

Songs + album covers + descriptions + embedded music.

Diary Entry

A more personal journal format with date, mood, photos, stickers and handwritten-style elements.

List

For example:

Things I Loved This Month
10 Songs on Repeat
Books I've Read
Places I Want to Visit
Quiz

Create magazine-style quizzes with questions, answers and results.

Moodboard

Upload images and arrange them into a collage.

Collection

Create collections such as:

"Things From My Childhood"

"Favourite Bollywood Songs"

"My 2000s Obsessions"

"My Art"

"My Bookshelf"

etc.

The architecture should make it easy to add more content types later.

ADMIN DASHBOARD

Create a /admin or similar private dashboard.

It should have:

Dashboard

Recent posts
Drafts
Published posts
Media count
Quick Create button

Posts

All posts
Drafts
Published
Create New

Media

Upload media
Browse media
Search media
Delete media

Categories

Create/edit categories

Site customization

Allow me to change things like:

Homepage featured post
Current song
Mood
Quote
About Me information
Favourite things
Featured photos
Stickers
Homepage sections
DATABASE / PERSISTENCE

The content must actually be saved.

Do NOT build this using hardcoded arrays containing fake blog posts.

Use a proper database/backend so that when I create a post, it remains there after refreshing the page.

Structure the application so it can eventually be deployed publicly.

Use appropriate authentication so only I can access the admin dashboard.

The public-facing website should be accessible to visitors without them having access to the admin area.

HOMEPAGE SHOULD UPDATE AUTOMATICALLY

The homepage should pull content from the database.

For example:

LATEST FROM SHANKIE'S

Automatically display my newest published posts.

PHOTO DUMP

Automatically display my latest photo dump.

CURRENTLY OBSESSED WITH

Editable from the dashboard.

SONG OF THE WEEK

Editable from the dashboard.

RECENTLY

Automatically show recent diary/blog entries.

So I can simply log into the dashboard, create something, publish it, and the website updates automatically.

MOST IMPORTANT DESIGN PRINCIPLE

Separate the CONTENT SYSTEM from the VISUAL SYSTEM.

I should be able to write a completely normal blog post in the admin panel, but when someone views it, it should look like it belongs inside an early-2000s teen magazine.

For example:

Admin:

Title: Things I Did This Summer

Text: ...
Images: summer1.jpg, summer2.jpg, summer3.jpg
Category: Life
Tags: summer, friends, 2026
Publish

↓

Public website:

A chaotic, beautiful magazine spread with:

giant colourful title
taped photographs
handwritten annotations
arrows
stickers
doodles
captions
little "OMG!" graphics
Y2K borders
Indian 2000s-inspired decorative elements

The content comes from me, while the website provides the visual language.

DO NOT MAKE THESE MISTAKES

Do NOT:

make a static portfolio
hardcode all the posts
use lorem ipsum
make fake buttons that don't work
make fake upload interfaces
create only a visual mockup
require me to edit code whenever I want to publish something
make it look like a modern Medium/Substack blog
make the admin panel inaccessible to a non-coder

I should be able to sit down, log in, click "New Post", upload my photos, write something, click Publish, and immediately see it appear on Shankie's.

The website is the magazine. I am the editor.
